      "postID": "5a546dcea17f6a503eb2c509",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "To be clear, Zarniwoop is requesting that the VRC_Mirror prefab have an object added to it, such as a UI Text object, so that when placed in your world, you'll see the text and it would warn the author about proper mirror usage and placement to avoid the common pitfalls, such as the mirror not being set up to face away from everything, or that it is generally a good idea to have the mirror off by default and have a local only trigger to enable it nearby.\n\nIt may be worth it to also have the mirror disabled by default in the prefab, and have a button included in the prefab so users don't even need to worry about learning how triggers work, they can have the button already there and configured in the prefab itself. It's easier to remove components/objects, than it is to set everything up correctly for someone new.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-01-09T07:22:54.173Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It's getting *seriously* frustrating exploring new worlds and most of them are unbearable to be in because of the damn poor mirror placements.\n\nI'm using minimum recommended specc for VRchat, VR mode in low pop instances and it keeps happening.",
